  "_doc": "What a session installs, and what it does not. Tier is a decision about attention and context budget, not about value. T0 is always cloned; T1 when working that company; T2 on demand; T3 is a consolidation candidate awaiting Frank's call. agents_md.state is OBSERVED from the working tree on observed_at, not aspirational — 'absent' and 'divergent' are defects this file exists to make visible.",

  "tiers": {
    "T0": { "name": "substrate",        "install": "always — every session, every harness", "rule": "Carries a contract other repos read. Losing it breaks the estate." },
    "T1": { "name": "revenue surface",  "install": "when working that company",             "rule": "Deploys to a live domain or holds a paying product." },
    "T2": { "name": "vertical",         "install": "on demand",                             "rule": "Real work, bounded scope, no live deploy of its own." },
    "T3": { "name": "consolidation candidate", "install": "never by default",               "rule": "No AGENTS.md, no CLAUDE.md, no distinct claim. Fold into a parent or archive. Frank decides — an agent never archives a repo." }
  },

